# Regex replace first-only versus global

Verifies the `g` flag controls how many occurrences `String.replace` rewrites:
without it only the first `a` in `aaa` becomes `b`, while `/a/g` rewrites all
three.

>>> source
const first_only: string = "aaa"->replace(/a/, "b")
print(first_only)
const all: string = "aaa"->replace(/a/g, "b")
print(all)

<<< stdout
baa
bbb

<<< stderr
